+# Implementation Plan: Hourly Rental
+
+**Branch**: `004-hourly-rental` | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Summary
+Add optional `hourlyPrice` to `Equipment`. Pricing/validation in `src/index.ts` distinguishes hourly periods (< 24h, on the hour) from day periods (midnight-aligned, as before).
+
+## Technical Context
+TypeScript, no runtime deps, tests with `node --test` (`test/rental.test.ts`). Single file `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Constitution Check
+`.specify/memory/constitution.md` is an unfilled template: no rules to apply. Gates pass.
+
+## Design
+- `parseInstant`: accept any whole hour (minute/second/ms zero) instead of midnight only.
+- `parsePeriod`: after end > start check, if duration >= 24h both ends must be midnight (day rental); else hourly.
+- `price`: hourly -> require `hourlyPrice` defined, total = hours * hourlyPrice (safe-integer check); daily -> unchanged incl. discount.
+- `addEquipment`: validate optional `hourlyPrice` (non-negative safe integer when not undefined); store it.
+- Conflicts/availability already use ms overlap; `availability` keeps using `parsePeriod`, so hourly queries work.
+
+## Project Structure
+src/index.ts, test/rental.test.ts (extended).
