+# Feature Specification: Hourly Rental
+
+**Feature Branch**: `004-hourly-rental`
+**Created**: 2026-10-22
+**Status**: Draft
+**Input**: User description: "Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon. Let customers rent by the hour. Equipment may have an hourly price (euro cents for one hour). A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the hourly price for each hour. An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour."
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*
+
+### User Story 1 - Rent a board for an afternoon (Priority: P1)
+
+Desk staff quote or book a rental of a few hours for an item that has an hourly price, and see a total of hours x hourly price.
+
+**Why this priority**: It is the whole feature.
+
+**Independent Test**: With a board at 8.00 EUR/hour, a quote from 13:00 to 17:00 shows 32.00 EUR, and booking it records 32.00 EUR.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** an item with an hourly price, **When** quoting a rental of under 24 hours starting and ending on the hour, **Then** the total is number of hours x hourly price.
+2. **Given** the same request, **When** booking, **Then** the booking total equals the quote.
+3. **Given** an item without an hourly price, **When** quoting or booking an hourly rental, **Then** the request is rejected.
+4. **Given** an hourly rental crossing midnight (e.g. 22:00 to 02:00), **Then** it is priced by hours (4).
+
+### User Story 2 - Hourly rentals respect availability (Priority: P2)
+
+A booked hourly slot blocks overlapping rentals of the same item, and the item shows as unavailable for overlapping periods.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** an item booked 13:00-17:00, **When** booking 16:00-18:00, **Then** it is rejected; 17:00-18:00 is accepted.
+2. **Given** that booking, **When** asking availability for a period overlapping it (hourly or whole-day), **Then** the item is not listed.
+
+### Edge Cases
+
+- Equipment added with an invalid hourly price (negative, fractional, not a number) is rejected; omitting it is allowed.
+- A free hourly price (0) is allowed.
+- A period of 24 hours or more is a day rental and must be midnight-aligned as before; non-midnight starts/ends of 24h or more are rejected.
+- A period not on the hour (minutes/seconds nonzero) is rejected.
+- Hourly rentals get no long-stay discount (they are under 3 days).
+- Day rentals (midnight to midnight) keep the daily price and discount, even for items with an hourly price.
+- Existing day-rental behaviour, validation and totals are unchanged.
+
+## Requirements *(mandatory)*
+
+### Functional Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: Equipment MAY have an hourly price, a non-negative whole number of euro cents.
+- **FR-002**: A rental of less than 24 hours starting and ending on the hour MUST be priced at hours x hourly price.
+- **FR-003**: Hourly rentals of an item without an hourly price MUST be rejected for both quote and booking.
+- **FR-004**: Rentals that are whole days from midnight to midnight MUST be priced as before.
+- **FR-005**: Other periods (not on the hour, or 24h+ not midnight-aligned, end not after start) MUST be rejected.
+- **FR-006**: Hourly bookings MUST conflict with any overlapping booking of the same item, and availability MUST account for them.
+
+## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*
+
+- **SC-001**: Every valid hourly quote or booking totals exactly hours x hourly price.
+- **SC-002**: No day rental changes price or behaviour.
+- **SC-003**: No overlapping bookings of one item can exist, hourly or daily.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- A midnight-to-midnight period shorter than a day does not exist, so periods are unambiguously hourly or daily; a 24-hour midnight-aligned period is one day at the daily price.
+- Times are UTC, as for day rentals.
+- Items without an hourly price remain day-only.
